The only solution I can think of is a magic whistle. Of course, you
don't have one. But if you could find one (in Minetown, say) then that
would solve your problem.

You could go get a magic whistle and a tripe ration. Come back. If he's
feral, feed it to him to re-tame him, then blow the whistle and presto!
Pet is now freed from the trap.

The problem is finding a magic whistle.  They are rare in the dungeon.


Question RE: Polymorph ... If you zap the cat with it might it lose
it's tameness and become hostile?  Facing off with, E.g., a master mind
flayer named Fuzzy on the first level of sokoban might be a cure worse
than the disease.

You can't kill your pet without risking divine anger and I'm assuming
you're not ready to deal with that. Hmmm... here's a nasty solution:

Go away until the cat becomes feral, then come back and kill it.  Then
grab a tripe ration (in my experience, common in Sokoban) and tame a
new pet (cats/dogs seem to be common in Sokoban and in Minetown).

